# XSH isfinite()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#

assertion  XSH.isfinite.001
anchor     functions/isfinite.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isfinite.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       isfinite() of 0, -0, 1, -1, 0.1, MIN, MAX and MIN/2 (MIN the smallest
           normal value, MAX the largest finite value of the type) is non-zero,
           for each of the three floating types.
test       t/001-finite.c

assertion  XSH.isfinite.002
anchor     functions/isfinite.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isfinite.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       isfinite() of +Inf, -Inf, a NaN and its negation is 0, for each of the
           three floating types.
test       t/002-not-finite.c

assertion  XSH.isfinite.003
anchor     functions/isfinite.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isfinite.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       For float and double, isfinite(MAX * 2), with MAX the largest finite
           value of the type, is 0: a product evaluated in a wider format is
           converted to the semantic type first.
test       t/003-semantic-type.c
